## Real Equipment, Real Troubleshooting: What Our Technicians Actually Fix

Generic "technical support" pages rarely name the equipment involved. Ours is not generic: our technicians are trained on our own gear, and the troubleshooting they do reflects the specific equipment in our catalog.

-   **Mixing consoles.** Our Soundcraft EPM-6 and Mackie Onyx 1640 consoles are what our technicians ride during live speeches, catching a hot channel or a dropped input before it reaches the speakers.
-   **DMX lighting.** Our Eurolite LED KLS-200 bars run on programmed lighting cues. If a cue does not fire as expected during calibration, that gets corrected before your event starts, not during it.
-   **Projector and screen sync.** Our Vivitek D5 series and Christie LX505 projectors are matched against Da Lite, Traulux and Projecta screens. A projector that will not sync to the right screen size or aspect ratio is exactly the kind of fault caught in the calibration phase above.
-   **Wireless microphones.** Our Audix Fusion Series wireless microphones occasionally drop a connection mid event, usually from interference or a battery running low. Our technicians carry the fix (a channel switch or a fresh battery) rather than letting your speech continue with a dead microphone.
-   **Fog machines.** Our Martin Magnum 650 fog machine needs its output managed against the room's ventilation and any smoke detection on site, particularly indoors.
-   **Staging.** Our GUIL modular stage platforms need to be level and secure before anyone stands on them, which is confirmed in calibration, not discovered live.

## Switching Between Multiple Presentation Sources

On MICE Pack bookings with more than one presentation source, for example a laptop for slides, a second laptop for a video, and a DVD player for a screened clip, our technician manages the switch between them using a Kramer VP-731, a 9 input video scaler, so the room's screen cuts cleanly from one source to the next without a visible glitch or a reboot. Our [video switcher rental](/blog/video-switcher-rental/) guide is the deeper, equipment first version of this section: the real unit, what 9 inputs actually means in practice, and which packages it is realistically available on.

To be clear about what this is not: this is a presentation switching tool for your screen, not a camera, recording or streaming system. Malaga Event Gear does not offer camera equipment, video recording, live streaming or broadcast services. If your event also needs simultaneous interpretation or an interactive voting system, that is not equipment we stock ourselves, but we coordinate it through a subcontracted partner. [Contact us](/contact/) if either applies to your event.

## Coverage Across a Multi Day Event

Technical support does not reset every morning on a multi day booking. On a two day corporate project for the agency Bmotion in Benahavis, our technicians monitored sound frequencies and video inputs continuously from an advanced control panel across both days, keeping input switching seamless and latency free from the first opening remark through the closing applause on day two. Read the full account in our [technical support for Bmotion in Benahavis](/blog/news-malaga-event-gear-delivers-flawless-audiovisual-production-for-bmotion-in-benahavis/) update.

