## FAQs

### What happens during my event? A quick coverage checklist

Calibration and testing before your guests arrive, live gain and signal monitoring while your event runs, on the spot troubleshooting if a microphone or projector fails, and teardown once your event ends. See [What Actually Happens During Your Event](#what-actually-happens-during-your-event-a-phase-by-phase-look) above for the full phase by phase breakdown.

### Is technical support for events the same as AV technician hire?

They cover the same crew from two different angles. Our [AV technician hire](/blog/av-technician-hire/) guide covers hiring the person: which package includes one, which charges extra, and how many hours. This page covers what that person actually does on site once your event starts.

### What happens if a microphone drops or a projector loses sync mid presentation?

Our technician fixes it in the moment, using the specific equipment we carry: a channel switch or battery change for an Audix wireless microphone, or a resync against the correct Vivitek or Christie projector and screen pairing. See [Real Equipment, Real Troubleshooting](#real-equipment-real-troubleshooting-what-our-technicians-actually-fix) above.

### Do you provide technical support for multi day events?

Yes. On a two day corporate project for Bmotion in Benahavis, our technicians monitored sound and video continuously from a control panel across both days rather than recalibrating from zero each morning. See [Coverage Across a Multi Day Event](#coverage-across-a-multi-day-event) above.

### How many crew members are on site, and how fast do they respond?

A dedicated technician is on site for the duration your package covers, watching the sound and visual signal chain directly rather than being called in after a fault is noticed, so a dropped connection or lighting cue gets caught and corrected immediately.

### Is the technician actively monitoring the event, or just on standby?

Actively monitoring. On the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) and [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/), the technician watches levels, video inputs and lighting cues continuously throughout the event, they are not a standby presence called in only if something visibly breaks.

### Is onsite tech support included in my package, or a separate booking?

It depends on the package, not a blanket rule: included on the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) and [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/), available as a paid add on on the [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/), and not offered on the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/). See [How Much On Site Coverage Do You Actually Get](#how-much-on-site-coverage-do-you-actually-get) above for the full breakdown.

### What is the difference between delivery only and full event coverage?

Delivery only, on the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/), means our crew delivers, sets up and tests the equipment, then leaves it to the DJ or host to run. Full event coverage means a technician stays on site actively monitoring and troubleshooting for the length of your event. See our [how audio visual rental works](/blog/how-audio-visual-rental-works/) guide for the full delivery process either way.

### Do you provide technical support for outdoor venues?

Yes, across Malaga and the Costa del Sol. Calibration for an outdoor venue includes the same signal testing as an indoor one, with extra attention to weather exposure and cabling. See our [audio visual rental for outdoor events](/blog/audio-visual-rental-for-outdoor-events/) guide for the specific considerations.

### Can your technician switch between multiple presentation sources during my event?

Yes, on packages with a large screen and more than one presentation source, our technician manages the switch between them (a laptop, a second laptop, a DVD player) using a Kramer VP-731 9 input video scaler, cutting cleanly between sources. This is a presentation switching tool only, not a camera, recording or streaming system. See [Switching Between Multiple Presentation Sources](#switching-between-multiple-presentation-sources) above.
